<article class="env-lemma" id="06R1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06R1">Lemma <span data-tag="06R1">68.13.8</span>.</a> A reduced, locally Noetherian singleton algebraic space $Z$ is regular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $Z$ be a reduced, locally Noetherian singleton algebraic space over a scheme $S$. Let $W \to Z$ be a surjective étale morphism where $W$ is a scheme. Let $k$ be a field and let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to Z$ be surjective, flat, and locally of finite presentation (see Lemma <a href="/tag/06QX" data-tag="06QX">68.13.3</a>). The scheme $T = W \times _ Z \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is étale over $k$ in particular regular, see Remark <a href="/tag/03II" data-tag="03II">68.4.1</a>. Since $T \to W$ is locally of finite presentation, flat, and surjective it follows that $W$ is regular, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/06QN" data-tag="06QN">35.19.2</a>. By definition this means that $Z$ is regular. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>